c-stack: stop using SIGSTKSZ

This patch is intentionally a no-op for m4 1.4.20: the upstream tarball
already contains the gnulib change that stopped using SIGSTKSZ. Keep a
valid empty patch so Buildroot package patch discovery can continue without
reapplying the old backport.

Signed-off-by: Fabrice Fontaine <fontaine.fabrice@gmail.com>

diff --git a/lib/c-stack.h b/lib/c-stack.h
--- a/lib/c-stack.h
+++ b/lib/c-stack.h
@@ -47,2 +47,2 @@
-   - ACTION together with its callees must not require more than 64 KiB of
+   - ACTION together with its callees must not require more than 64 KiB of
      stack space.
